Innovation JIIT 2.0 — Homepage Redesign Implementation Plan
🎯 Goal

Transform the homepage from a traditional college club website into a modern developer ecosystem that feels:

Student-built
Community-driven
Friendly
Innovative
Premium
Clean
Interactive

without losing any existing information or functionality.

Phase 0 — Code Audit & Setup (No UI Changes)
Objectives
Understand the current HTML structure.
Map CSS and JS dependencies.
Identify IDs/classes used by JavaScript.
Create a safe redesign foundation.
Deliverables
Homepage design system (CSS variables)
Consistent spacing scale
Color palette
Border radius scale
Shadow system
Animation timing variables
Accessibility improvements (focus styles, skip link)
Phase 1 — Global Design System

Create a unified visual language.

Color Palette
Background      #0D1117
Surface         #161B22
Cards           #21262D
Border          #30363D

Primary         #58A6FF
Success         #3FB950
Warning         #F2CC60

Heading         #F0F6FC
Text            #C9D1D9
Muted           #8B949E
Typography
Keep existing font initially.
Introduce a clear hierarchy:
Hero: 56–72px
Section Titles: 36–48px
Card Titles: 22–26px
Body: 16–18px
Spacing

Adopt an 8px spacing system for consistency.

Phase 2 — Navigation
Keep
All links
Existing routing
Existing JS
Improve
Sticky navbar
Glass/blur effect on scroll
Better spacing
Active link indicator
Smooth hover states
Mobile navigation refinement

No content changes.

Phase 3 — Hero (Most Important)
Objective

Create a strong first impression.

Preserve
Existing headline
Existing CTA buttons
Existing messaging
Existing functionality
Redesign
Split layout
Larger typography
Better whitespace
Improved CTA hierarchy
Developer-inspired background (subtle grid/dots)
Smooth entrance animations
Optional scroll indicator

This section defines the entire design language.

Phase 4 — About Innovation JIIT

Transform into a modern introduction.

Instead of long paragraphs:

Better typography
Two-column layout
Highlight key points
Add visual emphasis
Improve readability
Phase 5 — Domains / Activities

Convert activities into feature cards.

Each card includes:

Icon
Title
Description
Hover animation
Consistent spacing

Inspired by Hack Club's clean card layouts.

Phase 6 — Events

Modernize event presentation.

Instead of stacked content:

Featured upcoming event
Responsive event cards
Date badges
CTA buttons
Better hierarchy

Past events remain accessible.

Phase 7 — Innovation Spotlight / Projects

Present projects like GitHub repositories.

Each card contains:

Project title
Short description
Technologies
Category badge
CTA

GitHub-inspired, but unique.

Phase 8 — Statistics

Redesign using modern stat cards.

Each card contains:

Large animated number
Label
Supporting icon

Improve readability and visual impact.

Phase 9 — Gallery

Replace traditional layout with:

Responsive masonry/grid
Larger images
Hover zoom
Better spacing
Optional lightbox (using existing JS if possible)

Preserve all images.

Phase 10 — Team

Modern contributor cards.

Each card:

Photo
Name
Role
Social icons (if available)
Hover elevation

Consistent styling.

Phase 11 — Contact & Footer

Improve visual hierarchy.

Include:

Strong "Join Innovation JIIT" CTA
Contact information
Social links
Footer navigation

Keep all links unchanged.

Phase 12 — Motion & Micro-interactions

Introduce lightweight interactions:

Fade-in on scroll
Hover elevation
Button ripple/hover
Smooth scrolling
Animated counters
Card transitions

Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

Phase 13 — Mobile & Accessibility

Test and refine:

Mobile navigation
Touch targets
Responsive layouts
Keyboard navigation
Focus states
Semantic HTML
Color contrast
Phase 14 — Performance

Optimize:

CSS organization
Image loading
Animation performance
Remove unused CSS (only if safe)
Minimize layout shifts
Phase 15 — Final Review

Validate:

Visual consistency
Responsiveness
Accessibility
Performance
Existing functionality
Content preservation
Design Principles (Inspired by Hack Club, Not Copied)
Community-first: Showcase people, projects, and events.
Storytelling: Guide users from "What is Innovation JIIT?" → "What do we do?" → "How can I join?"
Generous whitespace: Let sections breathe.
Bold typography: Clear, confident headings.
Modern cards: Rounded, clean, with subtle shadows.
Developer-friendly feel: Use subtle code-inspired accents and badges, not a literal GitHub clone.
Meaningful motion: Every animation should support usability, not distract.
Files Expected to Change
innovation-2.0/index.html
Main homepage CSS file(s)
Homepage JavaScript file(s) (only where necessary for UI interactions)
Files That Should Not Change
Backend code
Other pages
Routing
APIs
Existing content and copy (unless you explicitly approve edits)
